Iterations (failures fixed in sequence):
  a) Rolldown could not resolve bare "react" import from the harness
     mount via resolve.modules → fixed by a symlinked
     tests/privacy/harness/node_modules so normal Node resolution finds
     workspace deps (git-ignored; rebuilt each run).
  b) pdf.js adapter emitChunk signature misuse → corrected to the real
     (Occurrence[]) => unknown callback; OCR keeps its (checkId,
     occurrences) callback.
  c) Report schema rejection: OCR reader description carried
     raster_dpi=0 → use the real output reader produced after
     rasterization (real DPI).
  d) projectReport source-identity error: supplied bytes must be the
     exact canary bytes that were opened → passed through verbatim.
  e) "ID: Duplicate identifiers" at export: OCR output re-emitted the
     raster transform → deduplicated by transform id before sealing.
  f) Warm-mode provenance: prepare() reports provenance=cache (the
     verified IDB slot); the opened handle then reports memory —
     assertions corrected to both real semantics; zero model refetch
     asserted.
  g) Prepared-offline run: browser emits request events for cache-served
     fixed assets (pdf.worker, standard fonts) with ZERO server-side
     hits → assertions moved to server log + request_failures; cold
     offline split into online-nav capture + post-setOffline capture;
     egress/storage collected before the context-destroying blocked
     navigation.
  h) Receipt embed of the raw document sha256 (itself a marker) →
     receipt now carries sha256_16 digests only; stale redacted capture
     copies wiped before the inspector writes.
  i) Dist literal census: vendored bundles carry inert literals
     (tc39.es, github.com repo links, xmlns namespaces, overridden CDN
     defaults, pdf.js parser test vectors) → check now fails only on
     telemetry/collector literals or literals also seen in runtime
     traffic; full census recorded in the receipt.

